 "group_of_questions": {
  "id": 29643,
  "group_variable": "Year",
  "graph_type": "multiple_choice_graph",
  "subquestions_order": "MANUAL",
  "description": "[GiveWell](https://www.givewell.org/) is a charity evaluator founded in 2007 that researches and funds highly cost-effective global health and development interventions, directing money through its own funds and recommendations to charities like the Against Malaria Foundation. In FY2024 it [reported \\$269.5M in total revenue](https://projects.propublica.org/nonprofits/organizations/208625442), nearly all contributions, and Coefficient Giving [has committed](https://blog.givewell.org/category/coefficient-giving/) to set aside \\$175 million in 2026 for opportunities GiveWell recommends. GiveWell's self-reported fundraising totals use a February\u2013January \"metrics year\" and include donations made directly to recommended charities, so they run well above the revenue on its own filings.\n\nAnticipated public offerings by AI companies, including Anthropic and OpenAI, would create substantial liquid wealth among employees with stated philanthropic commitments: all seven Anthropic co-founders [have pledged](https://www.transformernews.ai/p/anthropic-employees-philanthropy-billions-donations-effective-altruism-coefficient-giving-ai-safety) to donate 80% of their wealth and other employees have pledged shares worth billions more, with Anthropic matching those contributions. GiveWell has historically been a default giving vehicle for tech donors aligned with [effective altruism](https://www.transformernews.ai/p/anthropic-employees-philanthropy-billions-donations-effective-altruism-coefficient-giving-ai-safety), and analysts [expect a broader wave](https://www.forbes.com/sites/annatong/2026/07/26/chickens-pigs-could-be-big-winners-from-ais-300-billion-philanthropy-wave/) of AI-driven philanthropy in the coming years.\n\nA spreadsheet with the combined grants awarded through August 28, 2026 can be accessed [here](https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1kle3CW4c5iunhiRNqTaqpmVq8GYxvGpmfwJZs7F7sdI/edit?gid=0#gid=0).&#x20;",
  "resolution_criteria": "Each subquestion will resolve as the percentage change in total funds raised reported by [GiveWell](https://www.givewell.org/) in its [metrics reports](https://www.givewell.org/about/impact) for the corresponding metrics year, relative to its 2026 metrics year, computed as 100 \u00d7 (F \u2212 F\u2082\u2080\u2082\u2086) / F\u2082\u2080\u2082\u2086, according to GiveWell's published metrics reports.",
  "fine_print": "* GiveWell's metrics years run February through January, e.g. metrics year 2026 covers February 2026\u2013January 2027.\n* The relevant figure is the headline total that GiveWell reports for funds raised across all donation channels, including donations made directly to recommended charities that GiveWell tracks, as presented in its annual metrics report or equivalent publication.\n* If GiveWell renames or redefines its headline fundraising metric, the figure GiveWell presents as most comparable to prior years' funds raised will be used. If GiveWell publishes restated figures for the 2026 metrics year, the restated figure will be used.\n* Figures will be taken as reported in nominal US dollars, without inflation adjustment.",
